     "content_html": "<table class=\"unnumbered unstyled\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\" - 3x + 14 >  - 13\"></span></td>\n<td>This is the correct answer.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\" - 3x + 14 - 14 >  - 13 - 14\"></span></td>\n<td>Subtract 14</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\" - 3x >  - 27\"></span></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"\\frac{{ - 3x}}{{ - 3}} < \\frac{{ - 27}}{{ - 3}}\"></span></td>\n<td>Divide by –3 and switch the sign since you divided by a negative number.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"x < 9\"></span></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"\\left( {-\\infty ,9} \\right)\"></span></td>\n<td>This is interval notation.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n"
